The only explicit form constraint is that the piece be a game novel (游戏小说). Both candidates are fiction set in a game world with a college-student protagonist who plays an assassin, so both satisfy it.

For the holistic row, FIRST delivers a full arc: a hidden quest, an NPC power struggle, ancient history, the AI/reality theme, raids and a resolution. Its weaknesses are real. It is verbose rather than the concise, rhythmic prose requested, its mechanics are inconsistent (the 5-level protagonist is sent to 30–40 content), and the ending sprawls. SECOND matches the requested style: concise, rhythmic, and it explains its terms. But it is a short setup rather than a developed story. Its combat is a single paragraph, the high-difficulty raid and AI revelation are only promised ("零界幽谷", "才刚刚开始"), and it reads more like an opening fragment than a complete piece.


